Adapted from `CFSG/Quasithin/Chapter16/Section01To02/OtherPreliminaries/
JankoTwoHigmanSims/HSOuter/` for the intrinsic HS displacement theorem.
The original modules and their public interfaces are preserved. Original
ATLAS HSG1-p100B0 attribution is retained in `LICENSES/ATLAS.txt`.

# Fusion of the binary-family outer involutions in the HS normalizer

The generator signs give the parity of every binary product. For each odd
product not marked as an involution, a specified letter moves under its square.
For each of the 104 marked products, a checked conjugacy identity carries it
to one of the two fixed outer representatives. Its conjugator is a binary
product times one of ten explicit graph automorphisms; graph preservation
places the latter in the actual normalizer. Consequently every conjugator
normalizes HS. Symmetric-group cycle type is never used as a fusion criterion.

All finite equations are checked in Lean's kernel. `source/certificates.json`
and `source/discover.g` retain the witness data and discovery calculation.
Source: Aschbacher–Smith 16.1.5(10), printed p.1172; GLS3 Table 5.3m, 2C/2D.
-/

